{{Top|notoc=1}}
[[File:Delphidian-AlienArchive.png|thumb|right|200px|[[Delphidian]]s were a [[Sentience|sentient]] humanoid species.]]
{{Quote|Stop, humanoid!|Vanguard Axis member, to Omega|<ref name="Tribe">{{TBB|Tribe}}</ref>}}
A '''humanoid''' was an [[Species|organic]]<ref name="EncyclopediaZy">{{SWE|groups|zygerrians|Zygerrians}}</ref> or [[Droid|mechanical]]<ref name="EncyclopediaPro">{{SWE|technology|protocoldroids|protocol droids}}</ref> being that was similar in overall form to a [[human]]. Species like [[Cerean]]s, [[Twi'lek]]s,<ref name="EncyclopediaTwi">{{SWE|groups|twileks|Twi'leks}}</ref> and [[Mirialan]]s were humanoid lifeforms.<ref name="EncyclopediaLum">{{SWE|characters|luminaraunduli|Luminara Unduli}}</ref> Most [[protocol droid]]s were humanoid in shape.<ref name="EncyclopediaPro" /> That was also the case of the [[battle droid]]s used by the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], as the humanoid configuration allowed a better degree of versatility.<ref name="EncyclopediaBtl">{{SWE|technology|battledroid|battle droid}}</ref> The term was also used by a [[Vanguard Axis]] member to refer to [[Clone Force 99]] member [[Omega]], who ''was'' human.<ref name="Tribe" />

{{Species-stub}}

